`BigInt` is exact, cannot mix with `Number`, and is not JSON-serialisable:

```js
console.log(2n ** 64n);
console.log(7n / 2n, -7n % 2n);        // 3n -1n
try { 1n + 1; } catch (err) { console.log(err.name); }   // TypeError
console.log(1n == 1, 1n === 1, 1n < 2);                  // true false true
console.log(JSON.stringify({ n: 1n }, (_, v) => typeof v === 'bigint' ? v.toString() : v));
